title: 'Bug: ''view ID'' returns an empty view while another view on the connection shows that node as a replaced root.'
pid: 6956d9f4-47f1-4e7f-a117-a40b798fd793
body: |2-
  Steps: switch Top's 'to Jeff' to jeff-public's perspective, so its
  root is Jeff's fork '7642d4d5...'; then 'view 7642d4d5...' answers
  "The server returned an empty view; the graph may lack that ID."
  The server log has the request and nothing after it. Switch the
  first view back and the same command works. Reproduced twice, on
  2026-11-14. The server side is Drew's or Sue's; the message, which
  blames a missing ID, is the tool's, which is Cleo's.
